  "text": "jollof kingdom jollof was also another kingdom that arose in the senegambia region, founded by njaja ndiaye of walo. the title of the wollof kings was “burba jollof” meaning the supreme ruler. the jollof kingdom consists of six states kayor, baol, walo, jollof, sine and saloum. kayor, walo, and baol joined jollof through voluntary federation (association). sine and saloum joined through conquest, because they were originally serere states. the six states agreed to be united and made jollof as the metropolitan state (overlord). jollof, kayor, baol, walo and sine were all found in senegal region except saloum which was found both in senegal and the gambia. mbegan ndure was one of the “burba jollofs” who ruled jollof. jollof empire expanded during the times of biram ndieme koumba. factors that led to the decline and fall of jollof the fall of jollof started as a result of their contact with the europeans through some states like kayor, baol and walo, which makes them stronger to challenge the authority of jollof due to the help of the europeans. struggles for independence struggles for wealth jollof finally fall to its knees in 1560. [ diagram / map placeholder ]title: map of jollof kingdomdescription: map showing the jollof kingdom and constituent states including waalo, kayor, baol, sine, and saloum."
