       "The Serers are mostly fishermen who were believed to be originated from Kaabu's River Banks, They were believed to move from Cassamance region to cross into Foni, then finally to the North Bank Region, about 400years ago as a result of wars and insearch of fishing sites.",
       "The two Serers states in Senegambia were called Sine and Saloum originally called Mbissil.",
       "They called their traditional chiefs as “LAMAN”.",
       "They called their Nyancho kings /Nobles as GELEWAR ,eg; Mansa Wali Joh of sine and Mbekan Ndure of Saloum.",
       "They are believed to have the same ancestral origin with the Wollofs.",
       "Today, most Serers are found in Sine and Saloum, Jokadou, Niumi, Jollof, Baol, Cayor and also in the coastal villages of Kombo like, Brufut, Sanyang, Gunjur, Kartong, Tanji, etc, they live along the River banks to do fishing as their main Economic Activity.",
       "The Serer population is 2.9%. Of The Gambian population today, at (2013, census)"
