     {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "POPULATION AND DEVELOPMENT IN THE GAMBIA: Population of a country refers to the total number of people living in that country at a particular time. At 2013, The Gambia’s population was approximately 1.8 million ."
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Africa has a population of more than 1.4 billion, (at 2023) and the countries with the highest number of people in Africa are; Nigeria, Ethiopia, Egypt, Democratic Republic of Congo, and South Africa ."
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Population and housing census is conducted nationwide in The Gambia by THE GAMBIA BUREAU OF STATISTICS (GBoS) after every TEN YEARS. CENSUS / Head count is the general counting of people and houses in a place at a particular period ."
     },
     {
      "t": "ul",
      "items": [
       "Census can be DE-FACTO CENSUS (where only those present at the time of census are counted) or DE-JURE CENSUS (where only regular residents are counted, even if absent at the time of census) .",
       "Census started in The Gambia in 1881, but the first census in The Gambia after independence was in 1973, and since then it has been every 10 years. According to 2024 census, The Gambia is 2.4 million .",
       "The Gambia is divided into eight (8) Local Government Areas (L.G.A) namely: Banjul, Kanifing, Brikama, Mansa Konko, Kerewan, Kuntaur, Janjanbureh, and Basse .",
       "The Mandingos are the largest ethnic group (32.3%) followed by the Fulas (22.6%), at 2013 census .",
       "In 1993, The Gambia’s population was approximately 1.2 million .",
       "India and China have the world's largest population today .",
       "The population of the world today is approximately 7.9 billion people, (at 2023) .",
       "The next population census in The Gambia will take place in 2033 .",
       "K.M.C has the highest population density, while W.C.R has the highest number of people .",
       "The former Kombo North is the highest populated district followed by Kombo South, and Central .",
       "The scientific study of human population is called DEMOGRAPHY ."
      ]
     }
