  "text": "a tourist; is a person who travels to visit another place for pleasure/ a special purpose, while tourism; deals with providing accommodations, services and other activities connected to tourists . tourism started in the gambia in 1965 by a swedish called bertil herding, who came with 300 tourists. tourism today, is the second largest contributor to our economy. most tourists visit the gambia between october to may . in the gambia, most tourists come from united kingdom (england, scotland, northern ireland, and wales) and scandinavia (denmark, norway, sweden, finland, iceland, holland / netherlands, germany, etc) and the united states of america (u.s.a) . types of tourism & types of tourists types of tourism: recreational tourism, eco-tourism, sustainable tourism, pro-poor tourism, community tourism, cultural tourism, health and religious tourism, conference tourism . types of tourists: special interest tourist, sex tourist, business tourist, conference tourist, community tourist, health tourist, mass tourist . reasons why tourists visit the gambia to enjoy our warm climate to enjoy our beautiful sandy beaches our nature reserves e.g. abuko nature reserve gambia is politically stable (peaceful) for dating (marriage) in search of their roots and education historical and sacred sites / places the friendly nature of gambians the river gambia is navigable to travel gambia is closer to europe [ diagram / map / image placeholder ]title: welcome to the gambia landmark & sandy beachesdescription: photos of 'welcome to the gambia' landmark sign and tourists enjoying the sandy beaches . hotels, lodges, camps & restaurants in the gambia some hotels in the gambia : kairaba beach hotel, sunwing hotel, lemon creek hotel, sindola alla kunda, baoba holiday resort, paradise suites hotel, apolo hotel, ocean bay hotel, jungle beach hotel, bamboo village resort, tropic garden hotel, fajara beach hotel, bungalow beach hotel, cape point hotel, badala park hotel, prime atlantic hotel, palma rima hotel, coconut residence, kombo beach hotel, senegambia beach hotel, seaview beach hotel, kalimba beach hotel, bakadaji hotel, wood pecker resort hotel, novotel kombo beach hotel, kololi beach hotel, coco ocean resort & spa, sheraton gambia hotel resort & spa, tamala beach resort hotel, african princess beach hotel, kasumai beach hotel, balafon beach hotel, metzy residence hotel . note; a hotel is a building where rooms and usually meals are provided for people, in return for payment . a lodge is smaller in size and service than a hotel . a motel is a special park for vehicles, (eg; black and white garage, at busumbala) . a restaurant is a special place where you go to have a meal or drink . ocean bay hotel and resort, cape point bakau is owned by the state . the gambia tourism board is responsible for all matters relating to tourism . upcountry lodges and camps: tendaba camp (kiang), bird safari camp (janjanbureh), lamin lodge (lamin), sindola safari lodge (kanilai), kaira konko lodge (jarra soma), boboi lodge (kartong) . restaurants: sally’s restaurant, time less, ali baba restaurant, etc . tourist attraction sites / places in the gambia juffureh - home of kunta kinteh (n.b.r) sami karantaba tenda (c.r.r) wassu stone circle (c.r.r) fort bullen - barra (n.b.r) katchikally crocodile pool - bakau (k.m.) monkey park, bijilo (k.m) nature reserve in abuko, kanilai, etc kartong folonko - kartong (w.c.r) banjul (capital city of the gambia) sanementereng - brufut coastal fishing centres, eg; tanji makasutu cultural forest, brikama activities, tour operators & agencies activities / occupations connected with tourism: roots of home coming festivals, eco-tourism (bird watching), boat racing, transportation, aviation (airline companies), hotel services (bar keepers, waiters/waitress, entertainers, dancers, room attendants, security guards, tour guides, etc) . ground tour operators in the gambia: west african tours, discovery tours, african adventure tours, star tours, tropical tours, national holiday tours, gambia national tours, sunshine holiday tours . foreign agencies that fly in tourists: thomas cook (uk), thompson holiday (uk), the gambia experience (uk), awa tours (germany), spies (denmark), air tours (uk) . importance / benefits of tourism it provides revenue for government some give scholarship to gambian students it encourages inter-marriage [acculturation] it promotes local industries/ goods it discourages monopoly it encourages foreign exchange it encourages trade both locally and internationally it helps to preserve our culture disadvantages & problems of tourism disadvantages & problems of tourism problems / bad effects of tourism : introduction of new diseases e.g. hiv/aids, ebola, covid-19, stds encourages child sex trade trade in dangerous drugs, eg; kush some come to the gambia as spies it encourages prostitution (sex workers) some of their cultures are affecting our youth it encourages pick pocketing/ theft problems affecting development of tourism in the gambia : lack of enough funds to promote tourism inadequate transport facilities insufficient hotel facilities lack of enough promotion and sensitization on tourism and tourist’s behaviours most 'bumpsters' and online beggars makes life difficult for the tourist due to constant begging of recent, the outbreak of ebola in guinea, sierra leone, and liberia retard our tourism sector the outbreak of covid 19, also restrict the movement of tourist around the world note: -most tourist visit the gambia around october to december (tourist season), because that time is winter in europe when the temperatures are very low (cold), at europe . -most tourists don’t visit the gambia from may to october, because that time is rainy season in the gambia (too much of waters and malaria at that time) ."
